# Eastron SDM72CT-M.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Eastron SDM72CT-M — Modbus register map for Omni Console
# | 
# | Source: eastron-sdm72ct-m-modbus-protocol.pdf
# | - 3-phase 4-wire energy meter with CT inputs (5A secondary).
# | - Input registers (FC04), IEEE-754 float, big-endian (MSW first).
# | - All addresses are 0-based protocol addresses (register_number − 30001).
# | - Subset of SDM630MCT: no per-phase energy, no THD, no demand registers.
# | - Note: Energy registers 30073/30075/30077/30079 accumulate since last reset.
# | - Note 3: Total kWh/kVArh = Import + Export.
# | - Factory defaults: slave=1, baud=9600, 8N1.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Eastron
@model=SDM72CT-M
@vendor_website=eastroneurope.com
@description=3-phase 4-wire CT-connected energy meter — per-phase V/I/P/Q/S/PF, system totals, line voltages, neutral current, import/export energy (IEEE-754 float, input registers).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/eastron-sdm72ct-m.toml; Source: eastron-sdm72ct-m-modbus-protocol.pdf. Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
@x_origin=omniconsole

